@startuml sequence_diagram_module_integration
autonumber
title WEB01 - SD3: open a protected module in the shared shell

actor "Website user" as User
participant "BrowserRouter / AppShell" as Shell
participant "ModulePage / ProtectedRoute" as Guard
participant ConfirmedModule as Confirm
participant AuthProvider as Auth
participant authApi as AuthApi
participant apiClient as Client
participant "Back-End API" as API
participant "LazyModule / ErrorBoundary" as Lazy
participant "Feature page" as Page

note over Shell, Guard
Route registered only if a loader exists.
Viewer: EMPLOYEE or MANAGER.
Kitchen configurations and planning: MANAGER.
end note

User -> Shell : Open enabled feature route
Shell -> Guard : Match route inside AppShell
Guard -> Auth : Read shared session and required roles
alt Session still loading
  Guard --> User : Show permission check; keep protected content hidden
else No valid session or required role
  Guard --> User : Show sign-in or access-denied feedback
else Required role appears in shared state
  Guard -> Confirm : Mount guarded child
  Confirm -> Auth : refresh(expectedToken)
  Auth -> AuthApi : getCurrentUser(token)
  AuthApi -> Client : get("/auth/me", { accessToken })
  Client -> API : GET /api/v1/auth/me (Bearer)
  opt API responds
    API --> Client : Current user DTO or HTTP error
  end
  Client --> AuthApi : JSON or ApiError
  AuthApi --> Auth : Parsed user or error
  Auth --> Confirm : Session state with current permissions
  alt Role confirmed
    Confirm -> Lazy : Mount with load and ModuleRequest
    Lazy -> Page : Load and render on demand
    alt Import or render fails
      Lazy --> User : Section error and retry inside shell
    else Module ready
      Page --> User : Show feature inside the same layout
    end
  else Required role not confirmed
    Guard --> User : Keep the protected view unavailable
  end
end

note over Confirm, API
Protected error rule for SD2, SD4 and SD5:
when ModuleRequest receives a 401 or 403, ConfirmedModule
awaits refresh(expectedToken) before rethrowing the original ApiError.
The provider rechecks /auth/me via authApi and apiClient.
Other errors are rethrown without a role check. No request is replayed.
end note
@enduml
